==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
1525–35; from phrase ''by hear say'', translation of Middle French ''par ouïr dire''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-hearsay.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# [[information]] that was [[heard]] by one [[person]] about [[another]]
# {{context|legal|lang=en}} [[evidence]] based on the [[report]]s of others rather than on [[personal]] [[knowledge]]; normally [[inadmissible]] because not made under [[oath]]
# {{context|legal|lang=en}} an out-of-court statement offered in court for the truth of the matter asserted; normally [[inadmissible]] because not subject to cross-examination, unless the hearsay statement falls under one of the many exceptions

====Derived terms====
* [[double hearsay]]

====Synonyms====
* [[report]]
* [[rumor]]
* [[common talk]]
* [[gossip]]

